  "source": "WhisperX word boundaries; interpolated character positions",
  "pronunciationText": "Now all three constants. The task: find f prime of minus three. The function is f of x equals five e to the two x plus six. So k is five, ay is two and b is six. Copy the exponential, then multiply by k and ay. Five times two is ten, so f prime of x is ten e to the two x plus six. Now substitute minus three. Two times minus three, plus six, is zero, and e to the zero is one. So f prime of minus three is ten. On the graph, it's five high there with a slope of ten, twice the height, as ay equals two predicts."
